          "post_id": "531538",
          "text": "<p data-start=\"1706\" data-end=\"1804\">Let $f:\\mathbb{Z}\\times\\mathbb{Z}\\to\\mathbb{Z}$. Consider the following functions:</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-roman;\"><li data-start=\"1806\" data-end=\"1823\">$f(m,n)=4m+8n$<br>&nbsp;</li><li data-start=\"1825\" data-end=\"1841\">$f(m,n)=m-n$<br>&nbsp;</li><li data-start=\"1843\" data-end=\"1864\">$f(m,n)=m^2-n^2$<br>&nbsp;</li><li data-start=\"1866\" data-end=\"1888\">$f(m,n)=2m^2+2n+1$<br>&nbsp;</li></ol><p data-start=\"1890\" data-end=\"1936\">Which one of the following options is correct?</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li data-start=\"1938\" data-end=\"2048\">Only II is onto.<br>&nbsp;</li><li data-start=\"1938\" data-end=\"2048\">Only III is onto.<br>&nbsp;</li><li data-start=\"1938\" data-end=\"2048\">Only II and III are onto.<br>&nbsp;</li><li data-start=\"1938\" data-end=\"2048\">I, II, III and IV are all onto.</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
